@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+A customer who cancelled an order that used a single-use welcome code could not reuse the code on the corrected order: it was refused as already used. The README says a cancelled order gives its single-use coupon back; the code does not.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Cancelling an order releases its single-use coupon, so it can be used again.
+- Second report (free delivery at exactly €50.00): not reproduced on the current code. The rule "€50.00 or more, after every discount, before VAT" is already specified in `shipping` and tested, and was fixed in an earlier change. A €4.90 charge on goods that were €50.00 before discounts but below it after (e.g. a coupon) is correct. No change is made for it; support should check the order's goods amount after discounts.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `coupons`: add the requirement that a single-use coupon is given back when its order is cancelled.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/orders.ts` (cancel hands the coupon back under the wrong key, the customer instead of the order id), `test/coupons.test.ts`, `openspec/specs/coupons/spec.md`.
